<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">French protectorate of Laos</h1><p class="st-meta">1893 CE – 1947 CE · capital Vientiane</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The French protectorate that united the Lao lands east of the Mekong from 1893 and created the borders of modern Laos.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paknam-incident">Paknam incident</a> of 1893, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> forced Siam to cede the territories east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a>. The French explorer and consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auguste-pavie">Auguste Pavie</a> had already won the loyalty of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang">Kingdom of Luang Phrabang</a>. In 1899 the Lao territories were organised as a single unit under a résident supérieur at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vientiane">Vientiane</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> ruled the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Phrabang</a> as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and the rest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> directly, through provinces with French officials and Vietnamese clerks. Laos was a thinly populated backwater of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-indochina">French Indochina</a>, with taxes, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corvee-labour">corvée</a> labour and some <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> mining. Revolts by upland peoples such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hmong-people">Hmong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lao-theung">Lao Theung</a> broke out in 1901 to 1936.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> ended French rule in 1945, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lao-issara">Lao Issara</a> declared independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> returned in 1946, and in 1947 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-laos">Kingdom of Laos</a>, within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-fourth-republic">French Union</a>, gaining full independence in 1953.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-protectorate-of-laos.jpg" alt="French protectorate of Laos" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Laos_(1893%E2%80%931952).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1893 CE – 1947 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vientiane</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Auguste Pavie, Sisavang Vong</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lao, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/laos">Laos</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>French Laos, Protectorate of Laos</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=french-protectorate-of-laos" aria-label="French protectorate of Laos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7464 1511 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French protectorate of Laos lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7784 1767L5054 728M7784 1767L7939 2031M7784 1767L7754 1922M7784 1767L7756 1697M7784 1767L7894 1880M7784 1767L7788 1713M7784 1767L7784 1767"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M7939 2031h0M7754 1922h0M7756 1697h0M7894 1880h0M7788 1713h0M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7784 1767h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vientiane. <a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=french-protectorate-of-laos">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
